    "created_at": "2021-07-08T20:21:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-08T20:21:57Z",
    "body": "Thanks for pointing this.\r\n\r\nThis should be the `Window` an activation-gated API is called on/with, which in my understanding of the HTML wording should be the [incumbent](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-incumbent-everything) or [relevant](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-everything) object (depends on what a specific activation-gated API want).  Does that sound right?\r\n\r\nHowever, just saw the HTML spec warning right below those definitions that they \"should not be used by new specifications\".  Not sure which replacement terms we are supposed to use instead.",
